```

- Create a `views/` folder â†’ add `index.ejs` (same HTML boilerplate)
- Change `res.send()` to `res.render('index')`

## 3. Serving Static Files (CSS, Images, JS)

```js
const path = require('path');  // built-in Node module, no install needed
app.use(express.static(path.join(__dirname, 'public')));
```

- Create a `public/` folder â†’ subfolders: `images/`, `javascripts/`, `stylesheets/`
- In EJS: `<link rel="stylesheet" href="/stylesheets/style.css">`
- Don't write `/public/` in the path â€” Express strips that automatically

## 4. Dynamic Routing

For routes like `/profile/ved`, `/profile/veditha` â€” where part of the URL changes:

```js
// The ':username' part is a URL parameter â€” it matches anything
app.get('/profile/:username', function(req, res) {
  res.send(req.params.username);  // sends back whatever was in the URL
});
```

> **Workflow:** Type the URL you want in the browser â†’ figure out which part is dynamic â†’ add `:` before it in the route definition.

